    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d447">

                <pb facs="0657" n="557" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg557"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89/912</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to President Roosevelt
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-10-31">October 31,
                        1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. President</hi>: It occurs to me that
                    possibly you may care to have at hand the various suggestions for handling the
                    war debts which have been received here since the Department’s letter and
                    memorandum to you of May 22nd last. Some of the ideas are novel and seem to me
                    to be impractical; others are worthy of consideration. They include the
                    suggestions of Ambassador Straus, Ambassador Morris, Shephard Morgan, Judge
                    Manton of New York, etc.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d447-a1.xml" xpointer="d447-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
